---
description: Image links and image-buttons must not change appearance on hover unless explicitly requested
globs: "**/*.{css,html,js}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Image links — no default hover highlight

When adding or styling **image buttons** (links or controls where the hit target is primarily a photo, portrait, icon image, or clipping):

- Do **not** apply hover styles that change **opacity**, **filter**, **brightness/contrast**, **scale**, or **background** on the image itself.
- Hover may still change **cursor** (`pointer`, custom magnifier, etc.) and non-visual affordances (`outline` for keyboard focus only if needed).
- If a page needs a deliberate hover effect on an image link, add a modifier class (e.g. `--hover-fx`) and document it in the PR/commit; do not use the default portrait/link pattern.

Reference: `css/vantex.css` — `a.vantex-founder-portrait` and `.vantex-engineer-portrait a`.